original_question:
Write a Verilog module named `Multiplexer_2_1_parameterized1` that implements a 2-to-1 multiplexer.

The module interface should be exactly as follows:
```verilog
module Multiplexer_2_1_parameterized1
   (ctrl,
    D0,
    D1,
    S);
  input ctrl;
  input [0:0]D0;
  input [0:0]D1;
  output [0:0]S;
  // ... rest of the module ...
endmodule
```

The module should select the `D0` input and connect it to the `S` output when the `ctrl` signal is logic '0'. When the `ctrl` signal is logic '1', the module should select the `D1` input and connect it to the `S` output.
